  "body": "Stacked on #823 (on #802). Fork synced at v0.17.0. Retarget/merge after #823.\n\n## What changed\n\nA plate-mounted modular vise is now **two jaw-block fixtures** on a fixture plate's grid (#819), per the design note on #820:\n\n- **`modvise` (app):** `JawParams` (fixed or adjustable side; body length/width/height, jaw width/height/thickness, hard or soft insert, face offset, bolt diameter, bolt and pin footprint in the block frame, slot travel, slide) with a law refusing every nonsense figure by name; the solid (side profile of body + insert slab extruded across the wider of body and jaw - a conservative envelope, watertight); generic presets of our own round figures for 1 in 3/8-16, 2 in 1/2-13 and 50 mm M12 grids; and `fit_pair`.\n- **`PlaceModVisePair` (one undo step):** the fixed block on the named hole (a quarter turn: the pair runs along a grid row or column), the adjustable block (turned 180 degrees) on the same grid line at the hole nearest the stock that leaves a non-negative gap, slid along its slots by that gap so it touches the stock. Both are inserted through `InsertFixture`, seated by #823's own seat rule (hole, turn, standing on the top, on-the-plate law), and carry their place on the plate - so they are riders: moving the plate carries both, deleting it unmounts both.\n- **Refusals by name:** out of the slots' reach (hole, gap, travel), off the plate, a plate with no grid, no stock, stock in the fixed jaw / beside the jaws / under the plate / over the jaws, a bolt between holes or off the grid, pins without dowel bores, an off-quarter turn, two blocks of one side.\n- **Save/load:** one optional `mod_jaw` key on the fixture marker, read leniently like #823 (raw JSON, a key that doesn't read or breaks the law is dropped and logged, never a failed load). **When #830 lands, this key should move onto its `fixture_keys` reader.**\n- **MCP:** `add_mod_vise_pair` (plate, hole, preset, yaw, insert, per-block overrides incl. bolts/pins); reports both holes, slide, opening, fixed gap.\n- **UI:** a plate's Fixtures row gets \"Add mod vise pair…\" (preset, fixed jaw row/column, which way its jaw faces, soft jaws, Place pair); each block's row names its side, jaws and slide; jaw blocks don't offer \"Detect plate grid\".\n- **Plate edits vs. the stock (review fix):** `SetPlate` re-seats riders on their named holes while the stock stays put. It now refuses by name an edit that would put a mod vise block's clamping face into the stock (or deeper), with the block, its side and the depth (\"the plate edit would put mod vise '...''s adjustable jaw 16.000 mm into the stock - re-place the pair after changing the grid\"; `modvise::reach::face_gap`), and warns when an edit lifts a face off the stock (re-fit stays in #832). **It also clash-checks every re-seated rider, and the plate's new slab, against parts and stock, the way `MoveFixture` does** (`fixture_clash::after_fixture_shape`), and returns the by-name warning (`SetPlate::warning`, MCP `set_fixture_plate` `warning`). **This also closes the same gap for plain riders from #823**, whose `SetPlate` never ran the check (#823 is merge-ready and takes no pushes, so the fix lives here).\n- The placed-pair status line gives the slide in document units.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/820-mod-vises.md` (now also: plate edits vs. the stock, and `body_height` must cover the bolt heads - counterbored bolts).\n- **Split off:** the dual-station block, and edit/re-fit of a placed pair -> #832.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/mod_vise.rs`: `every_preset_block_is_a_watertight_solid_of_its_exact_figures` (exact bounds and volume, every preset, both sides, slid and not), `nonsense_block_figures_are_refused_by_name`, `a_pair_lands_on_the_grid_and_the_adjustable_jaw_touches_the_stock_at_every_quarter_turn` (holes, slide, fixed face on the near side and adjustable face on the far side to 1e-6, at 0/90/180/270; one undo takes both, redo), `every_refusal_is_named` (out of reach, in the fixed jaw, off-quarter, unknown hole, beside the jaws, same side twice, no grid, unknown plate, off the plate, no stock), `bolts_and_pins_must_land_on_holes`.\n- `crates/app/tests/mod_vise_plate.rs`: `moving_the_plate_carries_both_blocks_in_one_undo`, `deleting_the_plate_lets_go_of_both_blocks`, `the_blocks_are_judged_by_the_posting_gate` (a face pass strikes the jaws through `posting::verification_gate`; with 15 mm blocks it doesn't), `a_pair_survives_a_save_and_unreadable_keys_are_dropped` (round trip; an unreadable and a law-breaking `mod_jaw` key each dropped and logged, steel and place kept).\n- Review fix pins: `mod_vise_plate::a_plate_edit_that_pushes_a_jaw_into_the_stock_is_refused_by_name` (the review's rig - 60 mm stock, 770MX plate, 1 in preset, fixed C14, adjustable I16, slide 22.55: pitch Y - 2 refused naming the adjustable block and 16.000 mm, pitch Y + 2 refused naming the fixed block and 4.000 mm), `mod_vise_plate::a_plate_edit_that_keeps_the_jaws_clear_is_accepted_and_undoes_exactly` (pitch X + 0.2 accepted, no warning, undo and redo exact to the bit, a refused edit leaves nothing behind), `fixture_plate_riders::an_edited_plates_riders_are_clash_checked_where_they_land` (a plain block rider re-seated 4 mm into the stock gets the by-name warning; a clear edit is quiet; undo/redo exact). Both bite: with the new checks removed, each fails.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_mod_vise.rs`: `a_mod_vise_pair_is_placed_fitted_and_undone_over_mcp`.\n- `crates/ui` (CWD `crates/ui`): `fixture_modvise_tests::a_plate_row_places_a_mod_vise_pair_in_one_undoable_step`, `a_refused_pair_is_named_in_the_status`, `the_placed_status_states_the_slide_in_document_units`; the existing `fixture_*` ui tests still pass.\n- Existing suites re-run green: builtin_vise, fixture_plate, fixture_plate_riders, fixture_plate_detect, mcp_plate, mcp_vise; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` clean. No PNGs changed.\n- Linux quick gate: see the comment below.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The user's real mod vises on their real 770 XL plate (the generic presets are our own figures; the vendor STEPs were opened locally only to check the proportions are plausible, never committed or quoted).\n- Plates turned other than about Z, or grids with unequal X/Y pitch under a 90-degree pair (covered by the code path, not by a test).\n\nChangelog: Mod vises: place a fixed and an adjustable jaw block on a fixture plate's grid, the adjustable jaw slid to touch the stock, in one undoable step (MCP `add_mod_vise_pair`, Fixtures page \"Add mod vise pair…\"); a plate edit that would push a jaw into the stock is refused, and every fixture it re-seats is clash-checked (#820)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #820\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
